    "body": "@sb3nder it's a good point that they can still just prevent default but I think if you've got JS to do something extra then it's on you if the resulting behaviour isn't quite right. By \"odd behaviour\" I mean `data:text/html,<button commandfor=\"popover\" command=\"toggle-popover\">Toggle Popover</button><button commandfor=\"popover\" command=\"--custom\">Custom</button><div popover id=\"popover\">Content` for the given HTML if you open the popover and then click on the Custom button the popover remains open, but for essentially any other button you'd expect the click to close the popover element.",
